From 72e518a3f02acb5c50f2dc64d7ad844c4694908b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Li Jinpei <jinpli@amd.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 10:41:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] [AMDGPU] Use SCC branches for uniform truncates to i1

Low-bit tests can reach instruction selection as a truncate instead of a SETCC. The uniform truncate patterns already produce SCC, but branch selection only recognized SETCC and copied the condition through a lane mask and EXEC before branching on VCC.

Recognize one-use uniform truncates of i16, i32 and i64 when selecting a uniform branch. Keep the existing uniform-branch and one-use requirements, and leave divergent truncates on the lane-mask path. This removes the select and EXEC mask round trip without changing uniformity analysis or irreducible-cycle handling.

Assisted-by: OpenAI Codex
